  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "112-root",
    "title": "Towards better health for women and children in EA",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "AKU's Centre of Excellence in Women and Child Health and the Canadian Coalition for Global Child Health organised a conference in Nairobi, to discuss strategies aimed at reducing maternal and child deaths in East Africa.",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "03df585c1dfd5eff",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "112-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/112-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "Towards better health for women and children in EA"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Aga Khan University Centre of Excellence in Women and Child Health and the Canadian Coalition for Global Child Health organised a conference in Nairobi from December 3-5, 2015, to discuss strategies aimed at reducing maternal and child deaths in East Africa in light of the recently adopted Sustainable Development Goals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Professor Marleen Temmerman, Chair, Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology and Director of Women's Health, Faculty of Health Sciences in East Africa, spoke about the causes of maternal and child mortality and the interventions being put in place to reduce deaths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In an interview with a local television channel, on the sidelines of the conference, Dr Zulfiqar Bhutta, Director, Centre of Excellence in Women and Child Health, AKU, spoke about the role that communities play in securing mother and child health, and explained the importance of traditional health practices in improving health outcomes."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
